  "development_notes": [
    "Initial formatting during file creation reported a missing tests module; the file was then added. That individual formatter exit was not captured because the shell continued to a successful cargo check. Final format/test/lint gates all passed.",
    "Cargo.lock adds only the already-workspace-local keyweave-windows direct UI dependency; no new external dependency/version or network access."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Windows GUI native factory/conditional UI wiring has not been type-checked or run by a Windows compiler/runtime. Portable generic request driver with real Client machine is tested using scripted transport on Linux; not an actual Windows pipe/SDK/GUI test. Prior Windows native automatic approval quota rejection was not retried or bypassed.",
    "Windows transaction polling performs at most one transport method per frame without sleep/wait loops. Cold peer pin and individual SDK calls are synchronous on the same UI thread and are not hard realtime or guaranteed latency-free.",
    "Disconnect/endpoint switch invalidates display/Stop capability for old pending results but does not cancel an already submitted Stop. Default Drop cleanup is bounded; unresolved native flights/pins may be retained until process exit.",
    "The last observation remains visible with source/age after failure/disconnect but cannot authorize Stop until an accepted new observation. Closing settings never owns/terminates the host.",
    "Windows host discovery/launch UX, Start/Resume/Apply, devices/Event Viewer, actual desktop/accessibility/Chinese fonts, x64/x86 native SDK/pipe/host acceptance, Wayland, hardware and packaging remain incomplete.",
    "Default eight ignored IPC tests were separately actually run and passed, counted only in native_ipc. No actual keyboard capture, Hook/injection or global input recovery was tested."
  ]
